\ ============================================================
  ok\ ANS-style test suite - disassembler words DASM and DIS
  ok\ (DISASM=1 builds only). DASM sends the text of one instruction
  ok\ and returns the next address, so these tests check the length the
  ok\ decoder gives each encoding, including prefix pages, indexed modes
  ok\ and bytes that are not instructions (length 1). The text itself is
  ok\ sent to the terminal while the tests run; the displayed lines are
  ok\ the disassembly of each test sequence.
  ok\ Requires ttester.fs then 00_test_prelude.fs to be loaded first,
  ok\ in that order.
  ok\ ============================================================
  okMARKER M37
  okTEST-BEGIN
  okHEX
  okCREATE BUF 8 ALLOT
  ok\ SEQ ( c1 .. cn n -- )  store the bytes at BUF, c1 first.
  ok: SEQ BEGIN DUP WHILE 1- TUCK BUF + C! REPEAT DROP ;
  ok\ LEN ( -- n )  disassemble BUF and return its length.
  ok: LEN BUF DUP DASM SWAP - ;
  okT{ 12 1 SEQ LEN -> 1 }TNOP  Actual:Expected 1 =?= 1 
